The frozen semantics defines `sortVS` concretely as recursive insertion sort on integer lists, and `vsLen` as the usual zero/successor recurrence. The generated Lean value type has integer values but no runtime string-value constructor, so the faithful supported case here is exactly the task’s integer-list domain. I’ll implement stable insertion sort with the same `≤` branch for integers and a total, order-preserving fallback outside that supported domain, then prove length preservation structurally.
